[43.192255, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[43.229548, "o", "  HIGH  MODEL-01 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the model ships pickle-based weights\r\n                       models/suspicious-model: pytorch_model.bin: prefer safetensors (Module 9)\r\n  HIGH  MODEL-02 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the model points to custom code (auto_map or .py files)\r\n                       models/suspicious-model: modeling_custom.py ships with the model (read as text only, never run)\r\n  HIGH  MODEL-02 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the model points to custom code (auto_map or .py files)\r\n                       models/suspicious-model: config.json has auto_map (CVE-2025-66448 loaded this even with trust_remote_code=False before vLLM 0.11.1)\r\n  HIGH  RCE-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K --trust-remote-code lets the server run code that ships with a model\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: vllm: command has --trust-remote-code\r\n  HIGH  RCE-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K --trust-remote-code lets the server run code that ships with a model\r\n                       k8s: vllm/vllm: args have --trust-remote-code\r\n  HIGH  VER-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the engine version is in an advisory's affected range\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: ollama: ollama/ollama:0.1.33: CVE-2024-37032 (management API (/api/pull); fixed in 0.1.34; always: the digest from a registry manifest wasn't validated)\r\n  HIGH  VER-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the engine version is in an advisory's affected range\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: triton: nvcr.io/nvidia/tritonserver:25.03-py3: CVE-2025-23319 (Python backend; fixed in 25.07; always in the affected range (update the Python backend too))\r\n  HIGH  VER-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the engine version is in an advisory's affected range\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: triton: nvcr.io/nvidia/tritonserver:25.03-py3: CVE-2025-23320 (Python backend; fixed in 25.07; always in the affected range)\r\n  HIGH  VER-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the engine version is in an advisory's affected range\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: vllm: vllm/vllm-openai:v0.10.2: CVE-2025-62164 (inference API (prompt embeddings in the Completions API); fixed in 0.11.1; always in the affected range)\r\n  HIGH  VER-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the engine version is in an advisory's affected range\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: vllm: vllm/vllm-openai:v0.10.2: CVE-2025-66448 (model loader (auto_map remote code despite trust_remote_code=False); fixed in 0.11.1; when it loads a config that has an auto_map entry)\r\n  MED   VER-00   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the image isn't pinned to a version\r\n                       k8s: vllm/vllm: vllm/vllm-openai:latest: pin a version you have checked against the advisories\r\n  MED   VER-01   \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K 26.1 \u001b[m\u001b[K the engine version is in an advisory's affected range\r\n                       docker-compose.yml: triton: nvcr.io/nvidia/tritonserver:25.03-py3: CVE-2025-23334 (Python backend; fixed in 25.07; always in the affected range)\r\n"]
